      en: "Kuwait International Airport (KWI) is the main airport in Kuwait, located in Farwaniya, about 15 kilometers south of Kuwait City. The airport serves as a hub for Kuwait Airways and numerous international airlines. It was founded in 1928 as a small airstrip and has since developed into a modern airport. Terminal 1 is the main terminal, opened in 1998. The airport has a capacity of over 15 million passengers annually. KWI is known for its duty-free shops and lounges. The airport plays a crucial role in Kuwait's economy by facilitating international trade and tourism. Plans exist for a new Terminal 2 to expand capacity.",
